# AETHER: Universal Cognitive Context Layer and Graph Matchmaker

A high-performance universal context layer designed for hackathon ecosystems and developer platforms. AETHER ingests disparate, heterogeneous developer activity streams—internal commit velocities, hackathon submissions, peer reviews, and external digital footprints (GitHub, LinkedIn)—synthesizing them into deterministic cognitive archetypes, multi-factor reliability ratings, and a living relational knowledge graph. 

The context layer exposes these synthesized states through a bi-directional WebSocket stream, a live Cypher graph console, an autonomous squad matchmaking engine, a conversational intelligence agent, external integrations (Slack Block Kit and Telegram), and a terminal user interface (TUI).

---

